; The bird base's kite crease on the preliminary base: axiom 6 has two
; solutions through .c, but the outward one is a line meeting the base only at
; .c itself, cutting no face. The paper-incidence filter drops it and leaves a
; single survivor, so no `toward` is needed to reach the inward crease.

paper square

fold --bd = map .a onto .c
reverse --h = map .b onto .c
reverse --v = map .d onto .c

.o = free on --bd from .b at 1/2
--mid = through .c .o

.sr = free on --ab from .a at 1/2
reverse map .sr onto --mid through .c

; assert steps = 4
; assert faces = 8
